{"name":"Air Blue","hex":"#69a3c1","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"air","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Airoran."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The substance constituting Earth's atmosphere: a gaseous mixture of nitrogen, oxygen, and various trace gases.","The substance of the atmosphere seen as an agency of freshness."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/air"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Airblue","blocks":[{"text":"Airblue Limited is a private Pakistani airline with its head office on the ground floor of the Islamabad Stock Exchange (ISE) Tower in Islamabad, Pakistan. Airblue operates scheduled domestic and international flights, the latter to Saudi Arabia and the United Arab Emirates. As of May 2026, the airline serves three countries and 25 routes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Airblue_Airbus_A321neo.jpg/330px-Airblue_Airbus_A321neo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Airblue"},{"title":"Atmosphere of Earth","blocks":[{"text":"The atmosphere of Earth consists of a layer of mixed gas that is retained by gravity, surrounding the Earth's surface. It contains variable quantities of suspended aerosols and particulates that create weather features such as clouds and hazes. The atmosphere serves as a protective buffer between the Earth's surface and outer space. It shields the surface from most meteoroids and ultraviolet solar radiation, reduces diurnal temperature variation – the temperature extremes between day and night, and keeps it warm through heat retention via the greenhouse effect. The atmosphere redistributes heat and moisture among different regions via air currents, and provides the chemical and climate conditions that allow life to exist and evolve on Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Top_of_Atmosphere.jpg/330px-Top_of_Atmosphere.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atmosphere_of_Earth"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Airbus_A320-214%2C_Airblue_AN2243785.jpg/500px-Airbus_A320-214%2C_Airblue_AN2243785.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Airbus_A320-214%2C_Airblue_AN2243785.jpg/500px-Airbus_A320-214%2C_Airblue_AN2243785.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An Airblue Airbus A320-200","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAirbus_A320-214%2C_Airblue_AN2243785.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/AIrBlue_A340-300_AP-EDE_IST_27-Nov-2012.jpg/500px-AIrBlue_A340-300_AP-EDE_IST_27-Nov-2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/AIrBlue_A340-300_AP-EDE_IST_27-Nov-2012.jpg/1280px-AIrBlue_A340-300_AP-EDE_IST_27-Nov-2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/AIrBlue_A340-300_AP-EDE_IST_27-Nov-2012.jpg/500px-AIrBlue_A340-300_AP-EDE_IST_27-Nov-2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A now-retired Airblue Airbus A340-300 taking off from Istanbul Atatürk Airport","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAIrBlue_A340-300_AP-EDE_IST_27-Nov-2012.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Airblue_Airbus_A321-100_KvW.jpg/500px-Airblue_Airbus_A321-100_KvW.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Airblue_Airbus_A321-100_KvW.jpg/500px-Airblue_Airbus_A321-100_KvW.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Airblue A321-100","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAirblue_Airbus_A321-100_KvW.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Ise_building2.png/330px-Ise_building2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Ise_building2.png/330px-Ise_building2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Islamabad Stock Exchange Towers - Airblue's headquarters","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIse_building2.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikip